INT. CAROUSEL PAVILION, SEASIDE AMUSEMENT PARK - NIGHT

Dust sheets. Painted horses frozen mid-gallop, brass poles gleaming. A mirrored hub reflects a dozen flashlight beams.

SIMEON "SIM" ARCHAMBAULT, forties, wiry, kneels at the base of a lacquered unicorn with a pry bar. BEATRIX VON LOEWEN, thirties, mask pushed up, scans the pavilion with a handheld scanner.

SIM
(to himself)
Come on, come on, come on.

BEATRIX
Everyone's gone. Camera loops for six minutes.

SIM
(to her)
Then hold the light.

She obeys. He levers the unicorn's belly open. A hollow glints with gold coins, ancient, stamped with a stag, stacked like poker chips. Sim lifts one and bites it, and Beatrix lets out a long breath.

BEATRIX
(to the room)
Anyone want to say it?

SIM
(grinning)
It's real.
